        ('antenatal_contact', 'metric', 'Antenatal contacts', 'Antenatal care contacts -- a scheduled or opportunistic visit during pregnancy at which a health worker assesses the mother and fetus. Registered centrally; implemented only where a deployment captures a genuine per-visit antenatal chart.', null, null, 'tamanu', 'WHO_CORE_100', null, 'Antenatal care coverage is a WHO Global Reference List of 100 Core Health Indicators entry; the contact concept follows WHO recommendations on antenatal care for a positive pregnancy experience (2016) -- the ANC contact schedule, minimum eight contacts. This metric counts raw contacts; it does not compute ANC4+/ANC8+ coverage status, a downstream aggregation. Coverage against a population denominator is not materialised, the same numerator-only pattern as immunisation_dose (MAUI-6808) -- Tamanu holds no expected-pregnancies denominator.', 'count', 'visit', 'facility_id', null, 'bes-maui', 'draft', 'specs/dbt-model/metric__antenatal_contact.md'),
